elopments in the investigation into the suspected serial killer facing charges in Long Island`s Gilgo Beach murders.\par \par \uc2 Suffolk County Police say an arsenal of weapons was found yesterday inside Rex Heuermann`s home. He has pleaded not guilty to all charges and is on suicide watch as he is held without bail while awaiting trial.\par \par \uc2 Lilia Luciano has the story.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 LILIA LUCIANO: Neighbors who unknowingly perhaps lived among a serial killer for years flocked to the Long Island home of Rex Heuermann to watch police vigorously search for more clues on Monday, but have their own ideas about what should happen to the disheveled red house.\par \par \uc2 MAN: I think the village should probably act to take over the property and then tear it down.\par \par \uc2 LILIA LUCIANO: Investigators carried numerous boxes of the basement stairs leading out of Heuermann`s home. They say they discovered over 200 guns in a vault.\par \par \uc2 Heuermann is charged with a murder of three women and is also the prime suspect in the murder of a fourth victim. All of their bodies were found within a quarter mile of each other on Gilgo Beach in 2010, but Heuermann wasn`t arrested until almost 13 years later.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, New York State Police confirmed one of their investigators was the first to identify Rex Heuermann as a suspect in March of 2022.\par \par \uc2 MAJOR STEPHEN UDICE (Troop L Commander): This was the first time that Rex Heuermann name had come up.\par \par \uc2 LILIA LUCIANO: Court records show that Heuermann was first identified as a suspect after investigators discovered he owned a Chevrolet Avalanche, similar to the one a witness described when Amber Costello disappeared.\par \par \uc2 CBS News has learned that yesterday, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  recovered a similar make and model of that SUV in South Carolina, which they say is linked to the case.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT KOLKER ("Lost Girls" author): There has been 