r the gander.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s true.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: People watching \uc2 CBS\uc2 , I mean, they could pay us more.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I hope so.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE MILLER: Wow.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CHEN: Is that how it works?\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE MILLER: How about that?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All the cameramen and women, too. Y`all agree? Yes.\par \par \uc2 All right. Dr. Jon LaPook will be here to help us understand the use of artificial intelligence in medicine. Is it a good idea or is it a big time risk?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Do we owe you a percentage now?\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 **********************************(08:00AM, EDT)**********************************\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Welcome back to CBS MORNINGS. I`m Tony Dokoupil. Coming up in this hour, will artificial intelligence replace doctors? Experts say, probably not. But in our series "Age of AI," Dr. Jon LaPook looks at the potential pluses and minuses for patients.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE MILLER: I`m Michelle Miller. Actor, Sean Gunn has been outspoken on the picket lines as actors and writers strike. We`ll talk to him about what`s at stake only on CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`m Nate Burleson, author, Colson Whitehead is stopping by with his new book, "Crook Manifesto." He`s been called America`s storyteller. You know what? He`s definitely earned that title.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Two Pulitzer Prizes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE MILLER: Only one to do it back-to-back.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`ve got zero\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: But first, here`s today`s "Eye Opener at Eight."\par \par \uc2 MAN: Extreme heat is Arizona`s natural disaster.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The blazing heat refuses to let up for millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN STEELE: The Southwest will bake yet again, 