o take place tonight into early morning tomorrow, but I`ve got to say, this is one of three big weather headlines and I want to show you all of those. That`s headline number one, yes.\par \par \uc2 But we also have headline number two, a big winter storm that has created a lot of snowfall for the West. Now, we look at blizzard conditions from Winter Storm Alejandra up in the northern tier; on the warm side of this is our next weather headline. That`s where we`re going to have severe weather breakdown in part of the Midwest.\par \par \uc2 But let`s go back and talk about winter storm, or excuse me, let`s go back and talk about our big weather headline number one, and of course, that`s Nicole. Today is the last day to prepare. Hurricane Warnings from Daytona Beach down to West Palm. We could be experiencing hurricane-like winds as soon as tonight and tropical storm winds have already been felt on the Atlantic side of this thing.\par \par \uc2 It is so wide reaching, the storm surge warning is one of our greatest threats here, we can be looking at storm surge of three to five feet above normally dry ground. And that`s going to be a big problem for our beautiful beaches in Florida, and then it takes a turn to the north after it moves into the Gulf and it goes all the way up maybe even into your neck of the woods. We could be looking at big impacts for the Mid-Atlantic and even all the way up into the Northeast.\par \par \uc2 We know the highest wind threat is going to be down here in Florida, but that rainfall is going to be wide reaching.\par \par \uc2 Now, for the latest on Nicole, watch \uc2 The Weather Channel\uc2  on cable or live on your favorite TV streaming devices. Yes, Nate. Like I said even folks up in the Northeast should kind of prep for big rain and potential flooding as well.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: You know what, your right, my son`s football game on Friday was just moved to Thursday because of the weather. Jordan, I appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 Al