ing you to it.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, Vlad. We appreciate you. All right, well, listen, we`ve got a lot more on the battle to control Congress coming up in just a little bit, and that`s going to be with Minnesota Senator, \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 **********************************(08:00AM, EDT)**********************************\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Welcome back to CBS MORNINGS. I`m Gayle King. Coming up in this hour, the latest on the Midterms and who will control Congress. We will speak with Democratic Senator, \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I`m Vladimir Duthiers. Actor, Terry Crews is here with his new book for kids. It`s about the difficulties of growing up fighting for your dreams.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And I`m Nate Burleson. If you like to laugh while you`re rocking out, we`ve got you covered. The great "Weird Al" Yankovic, he puts down his accordion and talks about his new movie based on his life.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I do like to laugh.\par \par \uc2 But first, here is today`s "Eye Opener at Eight."\par \par \uc2 GOV. RON DESANTIS (R-FL): We not only won election, we have rewritten the political map.\par \par \uc2 JOHN FETTERMAN\uc2 : We bet on the people of Pennsylvania and you didn`t let us down.\par \par \uc2 JD VANCE (R) (Ohio Senator-elect): I will never forget the great people of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 JOSH SHAPIRO (Governor-elect of Pennsylvania): Because of you, our democracy endures.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: American democracy is alive and well. We`re following Midterm races all across the country as the results continue to come in.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT COSTA: The Senate still up for grabs after several key races went blue.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: The critical Georgia Senate race between Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is still