ar \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: And those were the big themes of the night.\par \par \uc2 Governor Hochul wanted to talk about abortion and Congressman Zeldin consistently brought it back to crime. By the way, Congressman Zeldin says he would not in fact seek to make abortion illegal in the State if elected.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: There`s a new focus on efforts to bring \uc2 WNBA\uc2  superstar Brittney Griner home after she lost an appeal of her prison sentence in Russia.\par \par \uc2 A Russian Court upheld her conviction and nine-year sentence for drug charges. After the ruling, President Biden said his administration is in constant contact with Russian officials about Griner.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Cordes is at the White House.\par \par \uc2 Nancy, good morning.\par \par \uc2 Are these talks going to get us anywhere or get her closer to coming home?\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: Nate, US officials tell us right now that those talks are not where they want them to be. And so at this point, it appears that Griner is going to be placed in even more punishing conditions than the ones she has endured so far.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 BRITTNEY GRINER (\uc2 WNBA\uc2  player detained in Russia): I want to also apologize for this mistake.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: Brittney Griner`s contrition didn`t sway a three-Judge Russian Appeals Panel. They upheld her nine-year sentence informing Griner via live video as she stood in her jail cell outside Moscow.\par \par \uc2 BRITTNEY GRINER: I`ve been hear almost eight months and people with more severe crimes have gotten less than what I was given.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Griner gets three, throws it down.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: The \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star who turned 32 in jail last week will now be moved to a labor camp, where according to the \uc2 US State Department\uc2  report last year, authorities systematically tortured inmates, in some cases resulting in death or suicide.\par \par \uc2 CHERELLE GRINER (Brittney Griner`s wife): BG is at her absolute weakest moment in life right now.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: Griner`s wife, Cherelle recently told Gayle King she feels Griner is losing hope.\par \par \uc2 CHERELLE GRINER: She`s like, you know, saying things to me like, "My life just don`t even matter no more."\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: The two-time Olympian who played in Russia during the \uc2 WNBA\uc2  offseason was arrested at a Moscow Airport back in February in the run up to Russia`s invasion of Ukraine for possessing less than one gram of cannabis oil.\par \par \uc2 BRITTNEY GRINER: IT`s been very, very stressful and very traumatic to my mental and psyche being away from my family, and not being able to communicate.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: It`s been about four months since the Biden administration first proposed a prisoner swap. Griner and another American, Paul Whelan, possibly in exchange for Russian arms dealer, Viktor Bout.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 : We`ve not been meeting with much positive response, but we`re not stopping.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: Griner`s legal team says it can take up to a couple of months for inmates to be transferred to a new facility in Russia and they say that Russian authorities may not give them a heads up before Griner is moved.\par \par \uc2 President Biden is expected to see \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , the Russian President next month at the G20 Summit in Bali. But right now, White House officials say Mr. Biden has no intention of meeting privately with Putin -- Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh, let`s hope there was some conversation going on behind the scenes.\par \par \uc2 We thank you, Nancy.\par \par \uc2 Police in St. Louis say that the 19-year-old who murdered two people at his former high school was carrying more than 600 rounds of ammunition for his AR-15 style rifle.\par \par \uc2 Orlando Harris is his name. He left a letter in his car calling himself an isolated loner who had no friends. In his rampage, he shot and killed a teacher and a 10th grade student before police found him barricaded inside a classroom and killed him.\par \par \uc2 Seven other students were hurt and the St. Louis Police Commissioner said this could have been much worse.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Now of the war in Ukraine and the Kremlin, which says this morning it will continue to make that claim that Ukraine is or may be planning to use a radioactive so-called dirty bomb on the battlefield. There is still no evidence at all, none, to backup that allegation.\par \par \uc2 Holly Williams is in Kyiv, that`s Ukraine`s capital.\par \par \uc2 Holly, good morning.\par \par \uc2 HOLLY WILLIAMS: Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Russia took its allegations about a so-called dirty bomb to the \uc2 United Nations Security Council\uc2 . The US has dismissed Russia`s accusations of a Ukrainian dirty bomb as transparently false.\par \par \uc2 The UK Ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  called it "pure Russian misinformation of the kind we`ve seen many times before." And Ukraine suggested that Russia could be laying the groundwork for a so-called false flag operation, accusing Ukraine of what it actually plans to do itself.\par \par \uc2 A dirty bomb is not a nuclear bomb and would be less harmful, but by using conventional explosives to spread radioactive material, it`s an effective weapon of terror.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, President Biden was asked whether Russia could be preparing to use a dirty bomb or even a nuclear weapon following its accusations about Ukraine. "I`m not guaranteeing you that it`s a false flag operation," he said, "But it would be a serious, serious mistake."\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has asked the UN`s nuclear watchdog to inspect two sites here that Russia claims are involved, though once again, it hasn`t given us any evidence of that -- Nate.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Holly Williams in Ukraine. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 US forces and their \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies are conducting their own military drills this week not that far from Ukraine. Chris Livesay went aboard a \uc2 US Navy\uc2  warship and got an exclusive look at an elaborate show of force in the Mediterranean Sea.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 CHRIS LIVESAY: We fly at dawn from the Southern Coast of Italy to join the USS George H.W. Bush aircraft carrier, a floating mountain of muscle flexing with more than 80 allied aircraft in international waters for \uc2 NATO\uc2  training, all set against the backdrop of Vladimir Putin`s repeated threats to fire nuclear weapons.\par \par \uc2 The Secretary-General of \uc2 NATO\uc2  has come aboard with a warning.\par \par \uc2 JENS STOLTENBERG (\uc2 NATO\uc2  Secretary-General): There will be severe consequences. It will be absolutely wrong if I went into the exact way we will react, but Russia knows that there will be severe consequences and we are vigilant and ready to react if something bad happens.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS LIVESAY: That something bad could be a dirty bomb, an explosive loaded with radioactive material. Russia now claims that Ukraine wants to use one on the battlefield.\par \par \uc2 Is Russia laying the groundwork for a potential false flag attack of its own?\par \par \uc2 JENS STOLTENBERG: We have seen before and that Russia has accused others for doing what they intend to do themselves. So therefore, we are sending a strong message to Moscow that they should not try to use a false pretext as an excuse for escalation of the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS LIVESAY: For now, \uc2 NATO\uc2  says its best weapon is overwhelming deterrence with a heart thumping display of firepower from fighter jets and helicopters to unparalleled surveillance, with tensions in the region at a fever pitch.\par \par \uc2 This may only be combat training, but if called upon, these fighters say they`re ready to strike.\par \par \uc2 But only to defend the Alliance, never to provoke Russia, they insist.\par \par \uc2 You`re the Secretary-General of \uc2 NATO\uc2  aboard a US aircraft carrier. Are you poking the bear?\par \par \uc2 JENS STOLTENBERG: We don`t seek conflict with Russia, but of course, when we see more threats, when we see a more dangerous world, it is even more important that we send a clear message to any potential adversary that we are there to defend all allies because that`s the best way to prevent an attack and preserve peace.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 CHRIS LIVESAY: And these aren`t NATO`s only exercises in the region. It is currently conducting nuclear weapons training elsewhere in Europe. Now, these are yearly events, but given the backdrop of the war in Ukraine, and now the fears of a dirty bomb, \uc2 NATO\uc2  says its focus has never been sharper - - Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes, they don`t want to be ready but they have to be ready. Chris Livesay for us in Italy.\par \par \uc2 Chris, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Coming up in just a moment, Kanye West`s antisemitic statements are a part of a long and ugly history resurfacing more and more in these United States, why the problem is much bigger than just Kanye`s comments.\par \par \uc2 But first, it is 7:17. Time to check your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Coming up: Could Rihanna be coming to Wakanda? Yes, please. We`ll show you the video that has everybody talking.\par \par \uc2 Plus, the story behind this photo. I love the story of a coal miner, courtside at a Kentucky game. Wait till you hear the backstory. You`re going to like it, too.\par \par \uc2 You`re watching CBS MORNINGS. We always thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: We want to really show you what it means to be a fan and a hardworking man. Take a look at this guy in the overalls. Okay, so this is Michael McGuire, who is a coal miner who came straight