emocrats running for Senate are pushing to change the filibuster to codify abortion rights, but unless Democrats win a 60-seat majority in the Senate, they will not have the votes to do that -- Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All right, all right, Weijia, Jack and Frankie`s mom, that first day back is always fun, getting back up on that bicycle, but you certainly know what you`re doing. Really good to see you. Thanks a lot.\par \par \uc2 WEIJIA JIANG: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Coming up next, Vlad Duthiers, he`s got the stories you`ll be talking about later today. Pretty soon, we`ll be welcoming Vlad back from baby leave, one of these days.\par \par \uc2 But first, it`s 7:43, time to check your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Oh, Vlad.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You just can`t stop your head.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I know. I can`t, but I`ve got to get to these stories because we have some really, really good stories this morning.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Let`s do it.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: So I`m going to just blast right into it. First an update on Iranian rock climber, Elnaz Rekabi.\par \par \uc2 We told you there was concern about her safety after she competed in South Korea without a headscarf. She returned to Iran overnight and heard this.\par \par \uc2 (CROWD chanting "Elnaz Champion.")\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Large crowds gathered outside of Tehran`s airport to give her a hero`s welcome, chanting "Elnaz Champion." She was also greeted by family members with some flowers. Check that out.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to state TV, Rekabi apologized to the Iranian people for causing tension that followed speculation she was signaling support for protests against Iran`s hijab laws when she did not wear a headscarf during her climbing competition on Sunday. There you see that photo, that video of her.\par \par \uc2 Rekabi told reporters today that she was busy putting on her gear and forgot to put on her hijab. Iran`s Embassy in South Korea denied reports that she disappeared after the competition.\par \par \uc2 Rekabi left the airport in a van. We don`t know where she went, but hopefully --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We still don`t know where she went.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: We still don`t know where she went.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That support says a lot.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: People are out there supporting her.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It does say a lot.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Good to see her\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Exactly right.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Also, the carefully worded explanation for why she wasn`t wearing the hijab says a lot as well.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Right.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I would still like to know more about what happened from the time she got in the van and got home because the concern wasn`t coming from us, it was coming from people who know her.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: The woman who died in police custody in Iran, Mahsa Amini has galvanized a movement in Iran. We will where it goes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes. And around the world.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Around the world.\par \par \uc2 All right, another movement that everybody is talking about, WNBA All-Star Brittney Griner. She just spent her 32nd birthday behind bars in Russia.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Oh, man.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Heartbreaking.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It is heartbreaking. So Griner`s representatives shared this message from her yesterday and this is very moving: "Thank you everyone for fighting so hard to get me home. All the support and love are definitely helping me."\par \par \uc2 You`ll recall that Griner was arrested in a Moscow Airport eight months ago. Authorities said she had vape canisters with cannabis oil in her luggage.\par \par \uc2 Last night, \uc2 NBA\uc2  superstar, Steph Curry took time out from celebrating Golden State`s NBA championship to support Griner. Listen to what he said during the Warriors` ring ceremony.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 STEPH CURRY: We want to continue to use our platform and the opportunity to shout out a very special member of the basketball community: Brittney Griner`s birthday is today. She is 32 years old.\par \par \uc2 We want to continue to let her name be known, and we pray that -- it has been 243 days since she has been wrongfully incarcerated in Russia. We hope that she comes home soon and everybody is doing their part to get home.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: And let me tell you, everybody is doing their part. There`s been a hashtag that`s been trending for Brittney Griner, #WeAreBG.\par \par \uc2 Billie Jean King tweeted support. Dawn Staley tweeted support. It`s a really big deal to have Steph Curry.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: LeBron James has tweeted support.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: . talking about this. Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But you know, when we interviewed Cherelle Griner, her wife a couple of weeks ago, she said one of Brittney`s biggest concerns, she talked to her in August was that people would forget her and think that her life didn`t matter.\par \par \uc2 So, it`s so important that she knows and they will tell her that we are still talking about her in this country.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That is right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She has not been forgotten.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: No. And in fact, she is saying in that message that you`re giving her life.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Right.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: By keeping her in your thoughts and your memories.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, I believe that`s true. I believe that`s true.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I agree as well. Yes.\par \par \uc2 All right, we are going to end with a record-breaking donation -- I love this story -- by billionaire/philanthropist MacKenzie Scott to the \uc2 Girl Scouts of the USA\uc2 . You all have daughters.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: You know what it is like when you`ve got to go out there schlepping those cookies.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Of course.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Right? Five dollar boxes. This is going to buy a lot of cookies because the Girl Scouts say the $84.5 million gift is the largest single donation in the organization`s history. The money will help the Girl Scouts expand diversity in membership and recover from the effects of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Since she is divorced, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  founder \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  in 2019, MacKenzie Scott has donated more than $12 billion.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: With a B.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: . with a B dollars, yes, benefiting more than 1,200 groups. Here`s just a few of the generous donations she has made just this year alone.\par \par \uc2 Back in August Scott gave two Beverly Hills Mansions worth a combined $55 million to the nonprofit, California Community Foundation. In March, she gave $436 million to Habitat for Humanity. And get this, she gave $275 million to Planned Parenthood, and in May she gave more than $120 million to the Big Brothers and Sisters of America.\par \par \uc2 Scott is still one of the wealthiest people in the world though, folks. According to Forbes, she ranked number 41 on the Bloomberg Billionaires Index with a net worth of more than $34 billion.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Even after all the giving, she still --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She still has got money.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: She still has got money.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: She deserves a round of applause for that.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She is using it for