d --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s scary.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Yes, it`s terrifying. And, you know, that`s when you kind of realize there is blowback to your material. And there`s been things that you know, I didn`t realize what happened, you know, I went after the Saudis, Jared Kushner, even Nobel Peace Prize winner, Malala doesn`t like me anymore.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Seriously?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Oh, yes. I told a joke. I said, she follows me on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , and I don`t follow her back. And the next day, she unfollowed me on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay, it is one thing --\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: This is real. This is real. Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: But it is one thing to deal with social media, but then when you`re receiving mail to your house.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Right.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Like, how do you deal with that?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I mean, yes, does that mean when you now write a joke, do you run it through multiple filters? One of those filters being, is this going to lead to me or my family being in danger?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Yes. I think one of the things that I think about now is, hey, you`re saying something is going to be in 190 countries and now because of the internet, everyone`s going to be able to see it. Do you stand by this?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: And the repercussions that may come with it.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: So, it`s like number one, is it funny? Number two --\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Absolutely, yes, and do I stand by it and the repercussions that could come with it.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But that`s the beauty of this special, which by the way, guys, \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2  who is a big cheese over at \uc2 Netflix\uc2  says it`s honest and then hilarious. He said one of the best specials he`s ever seen. \uc2 Reed Hastings\uc2  normally doesn`t speak out in that way. So kudos to you.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: CEOs love the special by the way, the CEO of OnlyFans twitted that she loved my cheeky jokes. I don`t know if she is talking about the jokes or she wants to see the cheeks. I don`t know.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: She is talking about the double tundra right there. I see what you did. I see what you did there.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: I don`t know.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But let`s talk about the joke you make about Kumail because I think this is hilarious, because you have serious stuff and then it goes to really funny.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Yes, he`s a cyber bully.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: He`s a cyber bully, because -- let`s put up the picture because you call him out on this thing. Don`t clap at this. You said, this is an insult to all brown people. Why?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: It`s a personal challenge, because he showed White people what we could look like and how dare he set the bar so high.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: You don`t have that underneath that?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: None at all. I`m barely filling this --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Under Freddy Krueger sweater, you don`t have eight-pack?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: No. I`m 165 pounds. So, I`m like trying to fill this up as much as I can.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Well, you might have heard that there is an opening coming up with Trevor Noah at \uc2 Comedy Central\uc2 . Have you already put in a call? Is anybody calling you? Are you even contemplating --\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Gayle, do you know something I don`t know? Because I`ve been hearing this.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I really don`t. I think a lot of people are dialing in to say, hey George Cheeks, think about me.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Word on the street there is an open seat.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Let`s put in the application right now because they`re going to revamp in January. How would you revamp?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Oh, that`s such an aggressive statement.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Well, first, we want to know if you`re interested.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Look, I`ll put it this way.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: I`m going to keep my DMs and my heart open.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: And one of two things is going to happen. Either "The Daily Show" is going to want me back or \uc2 OfficeMax\uc2  is going to want me back. But I will be exploring my options during the off season.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You were good in \uc2 OfficeMax\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: I was great.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: You were good. You were a good employee.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: I was hoping that you can get the Cannon Inkjet 5970 right now.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: But all jokes aside, when you heard that news, because it shocked all of us.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What was it like working from within and hearing that news?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: You`re talking about seeing Trevor`s dimples up close?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Because you guys see it in 10 ADP, I got to see it up close and -- he is an incredible talent, you know.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: He is.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: I got to work both with Jon Stewart.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: How about that?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Jewish Yoda and Trevor.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: International Man of Mystery. One of the funniest guys in comedy. I think, I am so honored to have been a part of that great American institution.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: And you know, if you think about "The Daily Show" and "SNL." Those are the two -- those are the two big ones.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But when you heard he was leaving, did you say "Yay?" Who can I call? Or did you say "Oh, I`m so sorry to hear he is leaving."\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: I actually -- I was -- I just -- I chatted with him. I`m like, man, I`m so glad you you`re doing it on your terms and you`re following your heart. That`s really what he wants.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Hasan, but listen, when a veteran receiver walks off the field, when I played, I went to his position. I told the coach, put me in the game. Okay. Are you saying --\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Oh, okay. Well, listen, I don`t -- I don`t have Shari Redstone`s number. I can I can give them a call. You guys know powerful people.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Let`s see how "The King`s Jester" does. Right? It`s a very funny hour.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: You`ve got two kids now. Does that change the way you do jokes? I mean, there are things that don`t qualify anymore?\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Well, yes, I mean, I definitely think about this. Everything I say is now going to be on the internet etched in amber. And so one day, my daughter is going to see what Daddy was saying.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, and also Beena is always watching.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Oh.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Yes. And Beena is always watching.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Count on Beena to keep you in check.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The internet remembers.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: A lot of pressure.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Thank you, Hasan. Good luck. Good luck whatever you decide.\par \par \uc2 HASAN MINHAJ: Thank you. Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That will do it for us. We will see you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Is your phone ringing?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Right here on -- he has a phone ringing -- CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright MMXXII CBS Broadcasting  Inc. ALL  RIGHTS  RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CBST000020221013eiad00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 New Details In Walker Abortion Controversy\b0\par\par\uc2 Tony Dokoupil, Nikole Killion, Gayle King \par \uc2 601 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2022\par \uc2 CBS News: CBS This Morning\par \uc2 CBST\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright 2022 CBS Broadcasting Inc. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: We`re going to turn now to the midterms in this country and some new developments in a few key races and we`ll start in the State of Georgia with Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 . The mother of one of his children tells "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " that he wanted her to get an abortion in 2009 and she had to push him to pay for it.\par \par \uc2 The Republican candidate who says he is antiabortion, very strict on the subject, publicly campaign yesterday with two top Senate Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Nikole Killion is in Atlanta for us following all this.\par \par \uc2 Nikole, good morning. They say they`re on Team Walker.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: Hey, good morning to you, Tony.\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is doubling down on his denials that he paid for a woman`s abortion although he now says he knows who the woman is.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 : I know nothing about an abortion.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: Republican Senate nominee, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  continues to insist reports he paid for woman`s abortion in 2009 are untrue.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC News anchor): Did you ever to your knowledge give money to pay for the cost of an abortion?\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 : No.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS: Is she lying?\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 : Yes, she is lying.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: Walker has expressed support for a total abortion ban and was asked to clarify his position.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 : I believe in life.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS: No exception.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 : Well, I believe in the Georgia Heartbeat Bill. You know, that has exceptions in it.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: But in a new report from "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ," a woman claiming to be the mother of his child says she had to press Walker to pay for the abortion he wanted. She claimed she told him "I can`t afford to pay for this," and said Walker sent her a $700.00 check by \uc2 FedEx\uc2  after the procedure.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 : You can see what they`re doing.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: The former football star tried to move on from the controversy as he teamed up with Republican Senators Rick Scott and Tom Cotton Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 SEN. TOM COTTON (R-AR): Let`s go elect \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  to the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: While they`re embracing Walker, GOP leaders and strategists are increasingly concerned his troubles could cost him in the pivotal Senate race CBS News has learned.\par \par \uc2 What do you say to those in your party who have concerns?\par \par \uc2 SEN. RICK SCOTT (R-FL): \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  led the dream of this country. He believes in this country and that is why people are going to vote for him.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: But some voters aren`t so sure.\par \par \uc2 MAN: There`s way too much baggage.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: I think he could do amazing things for our Senate.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  who once expressed concerns about candidate qualities says he plans to stick with Walker and speaks with him often. A new poll taken after the scandal broke finds that a Democratic Senator Raphael Warnock has a slight lead over Walker -- Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All right, Nikole, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright MMXXII CBS Broadcasting  Inc. ALL  RIGHTS  RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CBST000020221015eiac00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Heated Debate In Ohio\b0\par\par\uc2 Tony Dokoupil, Ed O`Keefe \par \uc2 501 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2022\par \uc2 CBS News: CBS This Morning\par \uc2 CBST\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright 2022 CBS Broadcasting Inc. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: We`re going to go now to Ed O`Keefe, who is covering a Senate debate in Ohio. It happened last night and Ed, it heated with Republican J.D. Vance and Democrat \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , both on the attack.\par \par \uc2 ED O`KEEFE: It sure did, Tony. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The race to fill an open Senate seat in the Buckeye State is among one of the closest this year making televised debates like the one last night and even bigger deal as they could tip the scales in either direction.\par \par \uc2 It could be feisty quickly on the economy, the opioid crisis, crime, how to deal with China, and political extremism. Ryan accused Vance of being too cozy with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . While Vance noted that Ryan`s voting record lines him up with President Biden and congressional Democrats most of the time.\par \par \uc2 Those attacks are going to be expected, but this exchange on abortion got especially personal when talking about the case of a 10-year-old Ohio girl who had to go to Indiana for abortion services due to Ohio`s six-week abortion ban that was in effect at the time.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 REP. TIM RYAN (D-OH): If you get raped, J.D. Vance and others are going to say you have to have that baby, State-mandated pregnancies for a rape victim. That is so far out of the mainstream, it is not even funny.\par \par \uc2 JD VANCE (R) (Ohio Senate candidate): That poor girl was raped by an illegal alien, somebody that should have never been in this State in the first place. You voted so many times against border wall funding, so many times for amnesty, Tim.\par \par \uc2 If you had done your job, she would have never been raped in the first place.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 ED O`KEEFE: That exchange in last night`s debate overall is emblematic of what our Battleground Tracker has shown, abortion is a driving topic for Democratic voters and Republicans like Vance are trying to keep the focus on crime, immigration, and the economy that fires up his conservative base.\par \par \uc2 And remember in Ohio, early in-person voting begins tomorrow, so does absentee voting. So a contentious debate like last night could be fresh on voters` minds.\par \par \uc2 Tony, now more than 15 States by the end of this week will be voting early or by mail. Election Day just 28 days away.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: A lot of contrasting policies and contrasting characters for voters to sort through.\par \par \uc2 Ed, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright MMXXII CBS Broadcasting  Inc. ALL  RIGHTS  RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CBST000020221014eiab000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Why Republican Leaders Are Rushing To Boost Embattled Candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\b0\par\par\uc2 Norah O`Donnell, Nikole Killion \par \uc2 729 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2022\par \uc2 CBS News: Evening News\par \uc2 CBSE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright 2022 CBS Broadcasting Inc. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NORAH O`DONNELL: Well, we are now just four weeks away from the midterms and Election Day. And one of the races that could determine the control of the Senate is in Georgia. Republicans are trying to help anti-abortion rights candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  fight off explosive allegations that he paid for a woman`s abortion in 2009 and then later fathered a child with her.\par \par \uc2 CBS\uc2 ` Nikole Killion is just outside Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION (voiceover): Former football star turned Senate nominee \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  teamed up with the Senate`s leading Republicans, Arkansas Senator Tom Cotton and Florida Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , making little mention of the controversy, framing it as an attack on him.\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  (R-Georgia Senatorial Candidate): You can see what they`re doing. They will do whatever it takes or say whatever they have to say, because they want this seat right here.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: While Scott and Cotton are embracing Walker, CBS News has learned GOP leaders and strategists are increasingly concerned his troubles could cost him in the pivotal Senate race.\par \par \uc2 What do you say to those in your party who have concerns?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR RICK SCOTT\uc2  (R-Florida): \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  led the dream of this country. He`s come from the ground up, from a small town with no money. He`s worked hard every day. He believes in this country. And that`s why people are going to vote for him.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: In recent days, new reports emerged that Walker, who opposes abortion, paid for the procedure for a woman in 2009, then urged her to have a second abortion. The woman claims to be the mother of his child and said Walker`s wife reportedly has texted her.\par \par \uc2 Today, Walker continued to deny the allegations.\par \par \uc2 (Clip of \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , ABC News Live Prime)\par \par \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2 : I know nothing about an abortion, and I know it`s a lie, and I said it was a lie. And I will just move on.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from ad)\par \par \uc2 MAN #1: "He threatened to kill us and had us move six times in six months."\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: A Democratic group backing Senator Raphael Warnock launched its first attack ad using statements from Walker`s son Christian, who lashed out at his father on social media last week.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from @ChristianWalk1R)\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIAN WALKER (Son of \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 ): Everything`s been a lie.\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: With early voting starting in less than a week, many voters are making up their minds.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: He`s a down-to-earth person. He`s not pretending. And, like he said, we all have a story.\par \par \uc2 MAN #2: Loved watching him play football, but he should not be in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: In a new interview tonight, Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said he`s been speaking with Walker often and plans to stick with him. Voters here in Georgia will get a chance to see Walker and his Democratic opponent, Senator Warnock, in what could be their one and only debate later this week -- Norah.\par \par \uc2 NORAH O`DONNELL: Nikole Killion, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Well, it was a terrifying scene today at a day care center in Allentown, Pennsylvania. A carbon monoxide leak sent nearly 30 children and adults to hospitals. Fortunately, all are expected to be OK.\par \par \uc2 Nine-year-old Danyelis Polanco said, when she got to the center this morning, she felt dizzy and that she knew something wasn`t right.\par \par \uc2 DANYELIS POLANCO (Student): I was a little worried, because I saw somebody from my class that was on the floor, and his eyes were closed.\par \par \uc2 NORAH O`DONNELL: Investigators say the leak was caused by a malfunctioning heater and blocked venting system. The building doesn`t have carbon monoxide detectors.\par \par \uc2 Believe it or not, there is no state law that requires a day care in Pennsylvania to have one.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright MMXXII CBS Broadcasting  Inc. ALL  RIGHTS  RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CBSE000020221014eiab000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; International\par \b \uc2 Russia`s Devastating Bombardment; Republicans Rally Behind Walker; Heated Debate in Ohio; Racist Comments Controversy; Hurricane Ian`s Lasting Impact; New Study on Colonoscopies; Army Announces Childcare Changes; View of Ukraine`s Battlefield; Daddy vs. Doctor; Dancing into History; \uc2 CBS\uc2  MORNINGS Deals, \uc2 CBS\b0\par\par\uc2 Gayle King, Tony Dokoupil, Nate Burleson, Charlie D`Agata, Nikole  Killion, Ed O`Keefe, Mark Strassmann, Jon LaPook, Manuel Bojorquez, H.R.  McMaster, Nancy Chen, Christina Ruffini \par \uc2 14,834 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2022\par \uc2 CBS News: CBS This Morning\par \uc2 CBST\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming Copyright 2022 CBS Broadcasting Inc. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Welcome, welcome to CBS MORNINGS on this Tuesday. I`m Gayle King.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I`m Tony Dokoupil.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And I`m Nate Burleson.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We`re all here. So, let`s go to today`s "Eye Opener." It`s your world in 90 seconds.\par \par \uc2 Russia bombs more targets in Ukraine after a brutal wave of missile and drone strikes that hit civilians during rush hour.\par \par \uc2 ADM. JOHN KIRBY (RET) (Coordinator for Strategic Communications at the National Security Council): More than 80 missiles and/or drones. The Russians can`t throw something like that together in just a couple of days.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Multiple LA City Council members have secretly recorded at a meeting where racist comments are used.\par \par \uc2 MAN: They`re sitting in a back room telling monkey jokes.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Just about every Senate race is neck and neck. The closest in Ohio where candidates squared off for the first time last night.\par \par \uc2 REP. TIM RYAN (D-OH): he was called an ass kisser by the former President.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: A new study could change the way we think of colonoscopies. We will tell you what you need to know.\par \par \uc2 DR. JON LAPOOK: An 18 percent lower risk of getting colorectal cancer, but no difference in dying from it.\par \par \uc2 MAN: A major rail workers union has rejected a new contract proposal raising the possibility of a nationwide railroad strike.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: Three people from a sunken fishing boat managed to fend off sharks in the Gulf of Mexico. Two of them were bitten on the hands.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Mahomes endzone. Who has got another? Travis Kelce, yet again.\par \par \uc2 MAN: A four-touchdown night for Travis Kelce, a new Monday night football record achieved. Hang on to winning.\par \par \uc2 MAN: I love this dude right here, baby. We keep fighting baby.\par \par \uc2 JAMES CORDEN ("The Late, Late Show With James Corden" host): A playset has gone viral for encouraging preschoolers to become, and this is true and equally depressing, \uc2 YouTube\uc2  influencers is a toy vlogger kit that includes a pretend selfie stick, camera stand and ring light and of course most importantly, a terrible relationship with your parents.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It is a joke, but listen, I think there`s a lot of truth in that.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: A lot of truth.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Three-year-olds and influencers, come on?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The best part of that toy is that it`s not made of plastic, so you can feel good about the purchase.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Come on.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What happened the Silly Putty? Slinky?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: "My Little Pony."\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: GI Joe with kung fu grip?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes. Lincoln Logs.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We could go on and on.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The list continues. Yes. Christmas is coming up.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Our age is showing.\par \par \uc2 Welcome to CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 We`ve got a big show today, very excited about this.\par \par \uc2 Comedian, Sebastian Maniscalco is here, along with his family pediatrician. That`s Dr. Scott Cohen to talk about their new podcast. Listen to the title, "Daddy vs Doctor." I like it. It is a lighter look at the challenges of being a parent with some medical advice thrown in as well.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Plus dancer, Chun Wai Chan is known for performing in some unlikely places. Now, he is leaping to new heights as the first ever Chinese principal dancer at the New York City Ballet. He speaks about his journey with our own Christina Ruffini and gives her a little dance lesson.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Christina shows off her moves, too. She`s got some.\par \par \uc2 But we`re going to begin with breaking news from Ukraine, which is facing yet another day of brutal Russian attacks. Multiple cities have been hit again today after dozens of missiles and drones were launched yesterday with targets all across the country. Many hit neighborhoods rather full of civilians at the height of rush hour.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian government says at least 19 people were killed by the first round of the strikes and more than a hundred injured. Charlie D`Agata is in Ukraine for more on the story.\par \par \uc2 Charlie, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: Good morning to you, Gayle. More rocket attacks overnight as you said, air raid sirens here and across the country. Zaporizhzhia targeted once again.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian military said more than 75 cruise missiles were fired into Ukraine, around 40 of them were intercepted, roughly two dozen Iranian suicide drones were used, too.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: This morning, Ukraine is still reeling from the onslaught, surveying the damage, counting the costs and the dead, an assault that sent residents of Kyiv back into subways and shelters, where they sang Ukrainian folk songs and the National Anthem in defiance.\par \par \uc2 (PEOPLE signing.)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: But while President Putin may have proved Russia has the reach and the recklessness to rain missiles down on civilians, his soldiers are taking a beating on the battlefield.\par \par \uc2 We traveled toward the frontlines in the south to Kherson where Ukraine`s troops have recaptured territory in a lightning counterattack measured daily by the mile. These villages were among the first to fall to Russia under its grip for seven months until they were liberated not much more than a week ago.\par \par \uc2 Oksana (sp?) was still in a state of disbelief.\par \par \uc2 What did you think when you first saw Ukrainian soldiers here?\par \par \uc2 (OKSANA speaking in foreign language.)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: "Happiness," she said. "I was just very happy." She fought back tears as she described life under Russian occupation.\par \par \uc2 We visited the high school that had been repurposed by Russian soldiers as a military headquarters.\par \par \uc2 The aftermath tells the story of the battle that took place here. Huge chunks of concrete taken out of the wall. Every windows smashed. The scorched buildings and the burnt out armored personnel carriers still bearing the "Z" of the Russian Army.\par \par \uc2 Where we found school teachers, Svetlana Resenchenko (sp?) taking stock of the filth and squalor that looked more like the remnants of a ragtag militia than professional soldiers.\par \par \uc2 (SVETLANA RESENCHENKO speaking in foreign language.)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: "When I came in and saw this horror," she said, "I still had faith that we will rebuild everything."\par \par \uc2 There is more rebuilding ahead and more fighting, too. Putin may have proven capable of destroying civilian life, yet his elite troops have proven incapable of even holding ground.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: Now, in addition to the air raid sirens, there have been new alarms that blast out on cell phones, including ours early this morning. Ukraine`s infrastructure is taking a real pounding. Businesses have been asked to shut down at 6:00 PM to conserve electricity -- Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh, the images are tough. Charlie, as you know, President Zelenskyy, he is going to make a brief appearance at the emergency G7 meeting later today. So, we`ll see if there is any help on the way.\par \par \uc2 We thank you, Charlie D`Agata.\par \par \uc2 And ahead, we will talk with former national security adviser and retired Lieutenant General -- there he is, H.R. McMaster about what these escalating attacks mean for the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: But for now, we`re going to turn to the upcoming election and two important Senate races that could decide who controls Congress come January.\par \par \uc2 Ed O`Keefe is tracking the Senate debate in Ohio, but first we`re going to go to Nikole Killian in Atlanta where Senate candidate \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is getting help today from two notable Republican senators.\par \par \uc2 Nikole, good morning to you. What are we learning?\par \par \uc2 NIKOLE KILLION: Hey, good morning to you, Tony.\par \par \uc2 And this is all about trying to shore up the candidacy of \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  in what is arguably one of the most pivotal Senate races to decide control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Senators \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  of Florida, and Tom Cotton of Arkansas will appear with the embattled Senate Republican candidate in a campaign stop here outside of Atlanta today. Walker, who says he supports an abortion ban without exceptions has been dogged by allegations that he paid for an ex- girlfriend`s abortion more than a decade ago. He has denied those allegations.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  also shares the campaign arm for Senate Republicans said that he is on Herschel`s team and is proud to stand with him. Of course, this all comes as the former football star is set to debate Democratic Senator Raphael Warnock later this week -- Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Looking forward to watching that. I know you are as well.\par \par \uc2 Nikole, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 We`re going to go now to Ed O`Keefe, who is covering a Senate debate in Ohio. It happened last night and Ed, it heated with Republican J.D. Vance and Democrat Tim Ryan, both on the attack.\par \par \uc2 ED O`KEEFE: It sure did, Tony. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The race to fill an open Senate seat in the Buckeye State is among one of the closest this year making televised debates like the one last night and even bigger deal as they could tip the scales in either direction.\par \par \uc2 It could be feisty quickly on the economy, the opioid crisis, crime, how to deal with China, and political extremism. Ryan accused Vance of being too cozy with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . While Vance noted that Ryan`s voting record lines him up with President Biden and congressional Democrats most of the time.\par \par \uc2 Those attacks are going to be expected, but this exchange on abortion got especially personal when talking about the case of a 10-year-old Ohio girl who had to go to Indiana for abortion 