d in football.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It is like the pendulum is now going to go all the way to the other side.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Exactly. I can`t grab Tony and say, "Hey, are you ready to go down right now?\par \par \uc2 NANCY CHEN: I am going to lay you down very gently.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s what the defenders are saying, they are saying, do you want me to lay down the offensive player like a baby in the crib?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s not what this game was built off. I`m not saying it has to be violent and we need to have collision after collision. I just feel like you can`t take that toughness and roughness and that greediness that made this game so special out of it.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CHEN: Well, but Nate, this is also comes right after the game that happened with that controversial call involving Tom Brady. So, what did you think of that?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I also feel like this wasn`t roughing the passer. Check it out. He didn`t slam Tom to the ground. It is a regular tackle. He gets up rolls over him, and then they throw the flag for roughing the passer.\par \par \uc2 I`m all about protecting the player. I`ll say that time and time again.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Right.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: But these penalties, you`ve got to pick those flags up. I think they will address this in the offseason for sure.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: So, why couldn`t there be a challenge from the other team and then a review and they take a closer look and they say, you know what, that was a fine tackle.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Because this is all about opinion.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Because they knew that they don`t have that.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: This is all about opinion. This is an eye test for the ref, so the ref can look at you and say I thought it was aggressive.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But now everybody is really focused on them, too.\par \par \uc2 NATE B